      "comboAudit": "All 80 combinations enumerated and screened for pt-BR vulgar/slur/anatomy/alcohol surfaces — clean. Codas restricted to r and z, the only letter-true final consonants in Brazilian Portuguese (final l vocalizes to /w/: sol reads sou; final m/n only nasalize the vowel: bom, sim; final-s monosyllables carry accents: gás, três, más). No c onset (c+u would surface cu-initial robot combos cur/cuz); no b onset (bar = alcohol venue). der (rare subjunctive) deliberately left robot and noted; puz/pez are archaic spellings, left robot. tez (complexion) and for (se eu for — everyday subjunctive of ser/ir) kept real.",
